44:    """
45:    Trace a green path from the start, turning right at pink controls and left at teal controls until it exits the grid.
46:
47:    Input structure
48:    - A black-background grid contains exactly one green start pixel.
49:    - The remaining foreground pixels are pink and teal one-pixel turn controls.
50:    - The green start has exactly one cardinal sightline whose first non-background pixel is a turn control.
51:
52:    Rule
53:    - Begin moving from the green start toward that visible control.
54:    - Paint green through background cells in a straight line.
55:    - When the next cell is a pink control, turn right without overwriting it; when it is a teal control, turn left without overwriting it.
56:    - Stop when the next step would leave the grid.
57:
58:    Key insight
59:    - The colored control pixels are not targets to fill; they are turn instructions for a single ray that leaves a continuous green trail.
60:    """
61:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
62:    bg = get_bg(g)
63:    colors = set(map(int, np.unique(g)))
